# The fleet installer's ingredients — the ONE place the Talos version and
# the official system extensions are spelled out. build.sh sources this;
# talos/hardware/*.yaml pin the image it produces (tag + digest) and point
# here rather than repeating the list. Bump Talos or an extension here,
# rebuild, repin both hardware files.
#
# Refs: https://factory.talos.dev/version/$TALOS/extensions/official
# (iscsi-tools + util-linux-tools are Longhorn's, ADR-0011. nebula
# 1.10.3 rode here from factory schematic 6a9acc… until Mesh v3 Phase 4
# P4.1 dropped it, 2026-09-21: the identity plane carries everything.
# kata-containers is the sandbox layer for agent workloads — spike
# bog2, decision 6d0u: registers the `kata` (cloud-hypervisor) and
# `kata-qemu` containerd handlers; k8s/apps/sandbox/ declares the
# RuntimeClass.)
TALOS=v1.12.6
OFFICIAL=(
  ghcr.io/siderolabs/iscsi-tools:v0.2.0
  ghcr.io/siderolabs/util-linux-tools:2.41.2
  ghcr.io/siderolabs/kata-containers:3.26.0
)
# Installer tag suffix after `<talos>-p0agent-<ver>`: bump when the
# OFFICIAL list changes without a p0agent release, so two installers
# with different contents never share a tag (the digest is the pin,
# ADR-0023, but a tag that lies is still a trap). Empty = none.
SUFFIX=kata
